not sure of the etiquette of these posts, but I know you only get to do
this once so I'm not going to miss out.
shrinker was the first priest I've played that got further than around
DL10, and what struck me was how much the BUC identification of items
helps get things moving along quickly.  his first good find was a
blessed scroll of identify which was used to discover a couple of
scrolls of taming on DL5 or so.  shrinker used the scroll on the first
tough monster he faced which turned out to be a soldier ant.  at around
the same time an egg he'd found on the dungeon floor and pocketed
hatched, and out popped a baby gargoyle that called out "daddy".
Zapping both pets with a wand of speed monster, and armed with a magic
whistle, he realised he had 2 very capable bodyguards to do his
bidding.  the mines cleared out easily with the ant/gargoyle combo, and
sokoban yielded a bag of holding.  An altar on DL11 and a wand of
wishing monster drop gave him what he needed to get further down the
dungeon: gray dragon armour and stormbringer.  The hungry black blade
unfortunately caused him to lose both pets eventually through rash
keystrokes, although he was trying to use his unicorn horn whenever
possible to avoid pet-kill.  Found Ludios on DL18 and jumped in, but
got zapped by a black dragon's disintegration blast and lost the armour
and priests robe.  Feeling a little vulnerable he skulked back to the
altar to enchant up some white dragon scales that had been saved as
backup.  he used the 2 remaining wishes to get a CoMR and SoR so that
his shiny white armour wouldn't get blasted again.  He had to use a
spell of jump to get across medusa's island, and found an Archon
waiting in the locked room next to medusa.  hastily reading a scroll of
taming, he teamed up with his new pet. When he reached the castle
realized the only way to cross was his amulet of magical breathing.
carefully putting all his scrolls and potions into the bag, he jumped
into the moat and started walking around to the back door.  checking
his bag he realized his stupidity as he now carried 20 or so scrolls of
blank paper and several potions of water. it wasn't all doom and gloom
though, as he found a spellbook of charm monster in the castle that was
to make him many, many recruits for the Archon's pet army in turns to
come.  He wished up boots of speed and a spellbook of Magic Mapping to
make Gehenomm less painful, and after drinking a potion of gain level
to get to L14 he ran off to do the quest.  Shrinker and the Archon made
light work of all the wraiths on the quest and returned with the Mitre
of Holiness at L21.  He ran straight back down to the Valley of Death
and decided that as he knew nearly 20 spells but had lost all the
spellbooks due to the water episode, no more time should be wasted
messing around.  The archon was valiantly killing anything that stood
in his way, until an innocuous purple worm stood in his way in
Juiblex's swamp.  "burp" was all he heard and shrinker had a sad
feeling.
Gehennom passed without incident, some demons were paid off, Orcus just
wouldn't die, and charm monster made him as many pets as master liches
would summon.  Rodney died to shrinker's only charged wand of death,
and upon entering Moloch's sanctum Dispater appeared next to him.
Shrinker and a few pets got rid of the demon easily and Shrinker
noticed to his delight that Dispater had brought the amulet of Yendor
straight to him.  taking it with glee he ran upstairs and headed
straight for the astral planes.  Rodney appear no less than 6 times on
the way up, as did several arch liches who made for a tough ascent back
up to the main dungeon. The planes were easy, and by the time Shrinker
made it to the Astral Plane he left behind some 30-40 pet elementals.
Famine stood in his way and went down with a death wand.  many priests
blocked the path to the first altar and when shrinker realised they
were not to be charmed, he pulled out a wand of teleport and began to
send them away.  After a hairy moment when he was down to 10 HP he
killed a summoned cockatrice and created many statues around him.  He
was in luck, that altar was Offlers, and after several minutes spend
gloating and doing nothing he grasped the amulet in both hands and
offered it, taking only a moment to blow his whistle to invite his 2
fire and 2 water elementals into the pantheons with him.

this was my first ascension, coming swiftly after a near miss when I
accidentally offered the amulet on the wrong altar when in fact trying
to perform a last minute conversion.  that experience made me realise
how tough the plane of air and astral plane were, so I was prepared
this time.  I didn't do any of thing things that I think abuse the
game: (nurse dancing, polypiling or taking advantages of succubuses) so
only had 100 HP or so.  got lucky with wishes and used 11 total, but
didn't polymorph or genocide at all.  I don't have a screen dump as my
apple mac tiled interface never gave me the chance, everything appeared
in popup windows.  ascension was after 49000 turns.  feels good to get
one at last :)

